      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence identifies two seq2seq shortcomings (overconfidence in predictions and incomplete/truncated transcripts when language models are used) and describes corresponding proposed solutions: neighborhood label smoothing (with uniform/unigram smoothing as background) to address overconfidence, and strategies to prevent incomplete transcripts\n— constraining EOS emission and adding a coverage term to the beam search criterion to avoid looping. This fully supports the question."
      },
